# Assignment 14 - TypeScript OOP Assignment

## UML Class Diagram

\\\mermaid
classDiagram
    class User {
        #id: number
        +name: string
        +email: string
        -password: string
        +phone: string
        -age: number
        +displayInfo(): void
    }

    class Admin {
        -permissions: string[]
        +manageNote(note: Note, action: string): void
    }

    class Note {
        +id: number
        +title: string
        +content: string
        +userId: number
        +preview(): string
    }

    class NoteBook {
        +id: number
        +name: string
        -notes: Note[]
        +owner: User
        +addNote(note: Note): void
        +removeNote(id: number): boolean
        +getNotes(): Note[]
    }

    class Storage~T~ {
        -items: T[]
        +addItem(item: T): void
        +removeItem(predicate): boolean
        +getAllItems(): T[]
    }

    User <|-- Admin : Inheritance
    User o-- NoteBook : Aggregation (1 User owns many NoteBooks)
    NoteBook *-- Note : Composition (NoteBook contains Notes)
    User <-- Note : Association (Note has author User)
\\\

## Relationships Breakdown:
1. **Inheritance**: \Admin\ extends \User\.
2. **Composition**: \NoteBook\ contains \Note\ instances.
3. **Aggregation**: \User\ can own multiple \NoteBook\ instances.
4. **Association**: \Note\ references \User\ as author.
5. **Generics**: Generic class \Storage<T>\.

